# Infrastructure

Terraform `>= 1.10`, AWS provider `~> 6.0`, region `us-east-1`. Remote S3 state
only — `terraform init -backend-config="bucket=$(../../scripts/state-bucket-name.sh)"`
(from env root; needs AWS creds). Commit `.terraform.lock.hcl`.

## Shared configuration (single source of truth)

**Set `project_name` in one file only:** `infra/common.tfvars` (copy from
`common.tfvars.example`). Every root loads it via committed `common.auto.tfvars`
symlinks — opening `common.auto.tfvars` in an env root is the same file, not a
second copy.

Also set in that file: `aws_region`, `github_owner`, `github_repo`,
`hosted_zone_name`, `certificate_domain_name`.

**Derived (never duplicate `project_name` elsewhere):**

- State bucket: `{project_name}-terraform-state-{account_id}` — Terraform
  `locals` use `data.aws_caller_identity`; init uses `scripts/state-bucket-name.sh`.
- Site FQDNs: `{project_name}-dev|staging.{zone}`, prod `{project_name}.{zone}` —
  `locals.tf` per env; optional `domain_name_override`.

Per-env `terraform.tfvars` = hardening only. Bootstrap-only vars in
`infra/bootstrap/terraform.tfvars`.

## Layout

- One `.tf` file per AWS service/concern under `infra/modules/static-site/`.
- New compute/API: new module + new `.tf` files — not inline app logic in HCL.
- `local.name_prefix` = `"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}"` for names.

## IAM

- No `*` in `actions`. No `*` in `resources` when ARN is known — comment exceptions.
- Use `data.aws_caller_identity.current` / `local.account_id`, not hardcoded accounts.
- GitHub OIDC trust pins `sub` to `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:<env>`.
- Policy changes: `depends_on` matching `time_sleep` with policy-hash triggers.

## S3 buckets

Each bucket needs: public access block (all true), ownership BucketOwnerEnforced,
SSE, versioning. Site bucket policy: OAC + TLS-only deny where applicable.

## Safety

- `prevent_destroy` on stateful resources; treat unexpected destroys as blockers.
- `terraform fmt -recursive` before commit. Variables/outputs need descriptions.
- No `# TODO` / `REPLACE_ME` in committed HCL.

## Commands

From `infra/envs/<env>`: `terraform init -backend-config="bucket=$(../../scripts/state-bucket-name.sh)"`,
then `validate`, `plan`. Never `-auto-approve` in prod.
